# React Router CSRF advisory (temporary)

**Delete this rule** (`.cursor/rules/react-router-csrf-advisory.mdc`) in the same change when you **apply** any of:

- React Router **Framework Mode** (`@react-router/dev` Vite plugin, `routes.ts`, server `action` / `ServerRouter`)
- **Unstable RSC** / React Server Actions via React Router

Until then, keep this file. Do not leave it in place after those modes ship.

## Why it exists

[CVE-2026-22030](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22030) / [GHSA-h5cw-625j-3rxh](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/security/advisories/GHSA-h5cw-625j-3rxh): CSRF on document POST to UI routes with **server-side route `action` handlers** (Framework Mode) or **RSC Server Actions**. Origin check can fail after the action already ran. Patched in `react-router@7.12.0` and `@remix-run/server-runtime@2.17.3`.

Vendor note: **no impact** for Declarative Mode (`<BrowserRouter>` / `<HashRouter>`) or Data Mode (`createBrowserRouter` / `<RouterProvider>`).

## Current project (not affected)

- Mode: **Data** — `createBrowserRouter` (web) / `createHashRouter` (Electron) + `RouterProvider` in `src/main.jsx` (no Framework/RSC, no server `action`s)
- Mutations are client-side (S3 / WebDAV / IndexedDB), not RR server actions
- Keep `react-router` **>= 7.12.0** (lockfile is already past this)
- Do **not** add `@remix-run/server-runtime` or Framework/RSC solely to “address” this alert
- Dismiss Dependabot/GHSA for this CVE while staying on Declarative or Data Mode

```text
❌ BAD — treat CVE-2026-22030 as a required app CSRF fix in BrowserRouter
❌ BAD — adopt Framework/RSC without deleting this rule
✅ GOOD — ignore the advisory until Framework/RSC; then delete this file and stay on react-router >= 7.12.0
```
